<title>NEW ZEALAND: Mainzeal sees NZ$6.5 mln yr profit, will pay div.</title>
<headline>Mainzeal sees NZ$6.5 mln yr profit, will pay div.</headline>
<dateline>WELLINGTON 1996-08-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>New Zealand property development, construction and investment company Mainzeal Group said on Thursday it was likely to report a profit after tax of NZ$6.5 million in the year to June 30.</p>
<p>It said this was a significant improvement on last year's NZ$2.8 million.</p>
<p>The company also forecasts that it will resume paying dividends again, after a break of two years, based on a &quot;substantial improvement&quot; in its earnings.</p>
</text>
